# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignore everything, then allow only what actually ships.
#
# This working folder accumulated a lot of scratch during development: frame
# dumps (ex_*, our_*, *_frames, pro_samples*), reference clones of other
# projects (openshorts_ref, aiys_ref, donkey_ref), downloaded model weights
# (models/, ~36 MB of third-party files), transcripts, render work dirs, and
# the old numbered attempts now parked in legacy/.
#
# A whitelist is much safer than a blacklist here: forget one pattern with a
# blacklist and you commit a few hundred MB, or someone else's source tree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*

# --- the program -----------------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!LICENSE
!README.md
!requirements.txt

# entry points
!make_shorts.py
!shortsmith.py

# pipeline modules
!transcribe_source.py
!highlights_heuristic.py
!highlights_llm.py
!diarize.py
# the local web UI
!webapp.py
!webui.html
!Start_Shortsmith.bat

# setup + verification
!setup.bat
!setup_env.py
!download_models.py
!doctor.py

# shared helpers

# launchers

# maintainer diagnostics
!tools/

# --- never ----------------------------------------------------------------
# models are fetched by download_models.py, and are third-party weights
models/
# other people's repositories, kept locally for reference only
openshorts_ref/
aiys_ref/
donkey_ref/
# the pre-existing attempts, kept locally but not part of this project
legacy/
# generated at runtime
python_path.txt
__pycache__/
# machine-specific settings (source video path etc.) - never ship these
local_config.json
